                            <comment id="495362" author="adilger" created="Tue, 2 Jun 2026 04:42:47 +0000">&lt;p&gt;This appears to still be failing regularly in interop testing with a new server and old client:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?client_branch=b2_16&amp;amp;server_branch=master-next&amp;amp;horizon=518400&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;source=test_sets#redirect" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?client_branch=b2_16&amp;amp;server_branch=master-next&amp;amp;horizon=518400&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;source=test_sets#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately I think this is a real interop issue and should not have been dropped from the 2.17 fix list.  It should &lt;b&gt;not&lt;/b&gt; be dropped from the 2.18 must-fix list without someone fixing it (and not just skipping the test unless they are sure that this is only a test script issue), since 2.18 will be an LTS and &lt;b&gt;lots&lt;/b&gt; of pre-2.16 clients will be interoperating with it..&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="422354" author="pjones" created="Thu, 25 Jul 2024 19:04:22 +0000">&lt;p&gt;As per discussion on the LWG call today, moving tickets that do not appear to be essential to fix version 2.17. If the fix lands before code freeze we will update the fix version to reflect that but we want to focus on activities on the critical path. Please speak up if you think that this issue definitely needs to be fixed before we could issue a 2.16 release.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="420057" author="paf" created="Sat, 6 Jul 2024 04:16:05 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Shaun,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since you debugged those, are you able to take a look here?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="420045" author="adilger" created="Fri, 5 Jul 2024 23:00:23 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Shaun, Patrick, any further thoughts on this issue?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are quite a number of different test failures related to UDIO changes on master, and I'm not keen on landing more of the HIO patches until the stability of the existing code is improved, particularly as we are trying to wind up the 2.16 release.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="417828" author="paf" created="Fri, 14 Jun 2024 16:06:06 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I will defer to Shaun for initial analysis, but if it turns out not to be a duplicate I can help dig on it.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="417822" author="pjones" created="Fri, 14 Jun 2024 15:45:38 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Shaun&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Is this a duplicate of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17927" title="sanity test_119e: FAIL: trivial unaligned dio failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17927"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17927&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Peter&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="417814" author="adilger" created="Fri, 14 Jun 2024 15:25:06 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=stancheff" class="user-hover" rel="stancheff"&gt;stancheff&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=paf" class="user-hover" rel="paf"&gt;paf&lt;/a&gt;,  is this a duplicate of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17927" title="sanity test_119e: FAIL: trivial unaligned dio failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17927"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17927&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17525" title="Unaligned DIO interop with different page sizes fails" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17525"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17525&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and will be fixed by the UDIO patches already in flight?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
